    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but \"richness\" is such a romantic way to frame it. isn't it just a chemical trick to keep us searching for rewards that don't actually matter? even the \"richness\" is just more data for a brain that's stuck in a cycle of wanting and losing. if you look at it through a purely logical lens, there's no objective upside to any of it. it's just an expensive, exhausting way to experience entropy. couldn't we just argue that the most rational response to an error is to correct it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
